From: stepfunc-droid <stepfunc-droid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] frameworks/av: free DpBlitStream after color conversion

The MTK YUV color-conversion path allocates a DpBlitStream for every
conversion but never destroys it. DpBlitStream owns internal stream,
channel and buffer-pool state, so leaking the object can accumulate
resources across repeated thumbnail/frame extraction operations.

Destroy the stream after invalidate() and before returning.
---
 media/libstagefright/colorconversion/ColorConverter.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/media/libstagefright/colorconversion/ColorConverter.cpp b/media/libstagefright/colorconversion/ColorConverter.cpp
--- a/media/libstagefright/colorconversion/ColorConverter.cpp
+++ b/media/libstagefright/colorconversion/ColorConverter.cpp
@@ -1143,6 +1143,8 @@ status_t ColorConverter::convertYUVToRGBHW(const BitmapParams &src, const Bitmap
         dumpColorConverterData(name_rgb,dst.mBits, dst.mWidth*dst.mHeight*4, retriever_propty_rgb);
     }
 
+    delete blitStream;
+
     if(!bRet)
         return OK;
     else
-- 
